      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T17:14:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] While I understand the intent to avoid noisy CVE tracking for a single header, replacing the `METADATA` file with a plain `README.md` completely bypasses automated license compliance and security scanning tools.\n\nConsider if there is a supported way in the `METADATA` schema to filter or scope CVE tracking, or consult with the security team before removing standard metadata from a `third_party/` directory.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "tag": "cl_review_agent",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "93af3eb45d11638dee8343dca2ff99674f012012",
